    "updated_at": "2021-05-17T23:54:57Z",
    "body": "The SSO provider has no reason to allow cross-origin requests to access the data it returns. And I'm not even asking for that data. The rule on credentialed redirects doesn't actually make any sense to me -- if the redirect chain ends in a CORS-eligible response, why does it matter that it went through a redirect to get there?",
